    {
      "text": "Ronin Bridge hack (Mar 2022) — illustrative teaching reconstruction, extended to showcase every investigator overlay. LABELED node addresses are REAL (Ronin Exploiter/Bridge, Tornado pools, Uniswap, Binance, USDC — click to open on Etherscan). The drainer / peel-hop / hidden-recipient addresses (0xbad…, 0xf00d…) are ILLUSTRATIVE PLACEHOLDERS, as are all amounts and tx hashes. Teaching aid, not forensic data. The Arbitrum One hop (0xf00d…0003 → 0xf00d…0004) is ILLUSTRATIVE too: the same address on two chains, linked as “same key” because it signed a transaction on Arbitrum. The 0xdec0…0001 address is an ILLUSTRATIVE exchange deposit address: funded by the root, swept to Binance 14 ten minutes later — marked \"likely deposit\" by the heuristic. The Polygon bridge example is ILLUSTRATIVE too: the root deposits 20 ETH into the Polygon PoS RootChainManager with depositEtherFor(0xf00d…0005), and 0xf00d…0005 receives 20 WETH minted on Polygon 30 minutes later — drawn as an inferred bridge link (high) to verify, never as a fact. The 30 ETH sent to the Polygon ERC20 Bridge has no candidate in the loaded data (Look row shown).",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -600
    }
